{
  "id": "bus-write-access",
  "title": "Bus write access (shared resource)",
  "chapter": "Use case 2 — Concurrent stochastic games: shared bus",
  "chapterOrder": 2,
  "formalism": "csg",
  "tool": "PRISM-games 3.x",
  "summary": "Two players concurrently read or write a shared object (buffer of size 1). The writer who succeeds wins; same action at the same time: no winner.",
  "description": [
    "Each player chooses, at the same time and without knowing the other's choice, to write (w), read (r) or keep the bus unlocked (unlock). A non-player Monitor (CommunicationBus) records the outcome in win.",
    "(w1, r2) gives the bus to player 1 (win = 1, +1 for player 1, −1 for player 2); (r1, w2) gives it to player 2; (w1, w2) and (r1, r2) end with no winner. (reset_1, reset_2) brings the game back to s = 0.",
    "The rounds module counts the rounds; k bounds the horizon of the properties."
  ],
  "objectives": [
    "Write concurrent joint actions [a1, a2] in a non-player module.",
    "Use rPATL coalitions: what can a player guarantee alone, and with a partner?",
    "Read action rewards as utilities."
  ],
  "exercises": [
    "Predict first: which of <<p1>> Pmax=? [F win=1] and <<p1,p2>> Pmax=? [F win=1] is 0? Then check.",
    "Compute the utility player 1 can guarantee over k rounds, then vary k.",
    "Add a third player p3: how many monitor commands do you need? How does the state space grow?"
  ],
  "parameters": [
    {
      "name": "k",
      "label": "Number of rounds",
      "value": "10",
      "description": "Horizon used by the rounds module and by the bounded properties"
    }
  ],
